# MCP token budget

Keep sessions cheap. Prefer structured MCP lookups over dumping trees into chat.

## Prefer

| MCP | Use for |
|---|---|
| **jcodemunch** | After the repo is indexed: `search_symbols`, `get_context_bundle`, `get_file_outline`, `assemble_task_context`, `get_session_context` instead of broad Grep/Read/Glob sweeps |
| **cursor10x-mcp** | `initConversation`, `storeMilestone` / `storeDecision` / `storeRequirement`, `getComprehensiveContext` at session boundaries |
| **Context7** | Current Rust, wasm-bindgen, Vite, Playwright API docs |
| **desktop-commander** | Long builds/tests or surgical file ops when useful |

## Avoid

- Pasting whole crates or large file dumps into chat when jcodemunch can answer
- Re-stating milestone status every turn when cursor10x already stores it
- Guessing library APIs when Context7 can resolve them
- Replacing normal `git` / `cargo` flow with desktop-commander for routine work
- Duplicating `plan.md` content into user-memory

## Session pattern

```text
cursor10x initConversation
→ jcodemunch get_session_context / assemble_task_context (once indexed)
→ next-slice skill
→ Plan Mode → implement → quality-gate
→ cursor10x storeMilestone / endConversation
```

Re-index with jcodemunch (`index_folder`) after each meaningful merge or when symbols drift.
